  "description": "(opt18) Spider:\r\n\r\nIn the solitaire game \"Spider solitaire\" stacks of cards of the same suit can be moved\r\nfrom a pile to another and cards can be placed on a card with a value that is higher by\r\none (of any suit). In contrast to the real game, all cards are face-up from the start, to\r\nremove uncertainty. Movement of stacks of cards could be easily modeled with derived\r\npredicates but here we use auxiliary 0-cost actions that update the state.",
